-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Moses</surname><given-names>SN</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Schizophrenia diagnosis and anterior hippocampal volume make separate contributions to sensory gating.</article-title><source>Psychophysiology</source><volume>45</volume><fpage>926</fpage><lpage>935</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18823427</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004811-Salmelin1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Salmelin</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Service</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiesila</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Uutela</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Salonen</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Impaired visual word processing in dyslexia revealed with magnetoencephalography.</article-title><source>Ann Neurol</source><volume>40</volume><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>162</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8773596</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004811-LajinessONeill1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lajiness-O'Neill</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Akamine</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Bowyer</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Treatment effects of Fast ForWord demonstrated by magnetoencephalography (MEG) in a child with developmental dyslexia.</article-title><source>Neurocase</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>390</fpage><lpage>401</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18781438</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004811-TovarSpinoza1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tovar-Spinoza</surname><given